{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794586013082,"sessionID":"ses_e2a5adb61ffe5JLlq3JICE94gJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5a96be2001ZHG1QqkdYKwWMe","sessionID":"ses_e2a5adb61ffe5JLlq3JICE94gJ","messageID":"msg_1d5a93144001tAi3VtHKAsX320","type":"tool","id":"call_199987ab4f30494fb4c80802","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog/v2.10.0.0.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog/v2.10.0.0.md, lines 1-91\n1: ---\n2: title: \"sk-doc v2.10.0.0, the create skill command is now sk-skill\"\n3: description: \"v2.10.0.0 renames `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime with no alias, so no command file is named `skill.md` and Claude Code lists all 44 tracked commands.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"sk-doc v2.10.0.0\"\n6:   - \"sk-doc 2.10.0.0\"\n7:   - \"create skill command rename\"\n8:   - \"sk-skill command name\"\n9: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n10: contextType: \"general\"\n11: version: 2.10.0.0\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # v2.10.0.0, The Create Skill Command Is Now sk-skill\n15: \n16: `/create:skill` is now `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime, with no alias. The old file name caused the bug. A command file named `skill.md` makes Claude Code read its folder as one skill. Every other command in that folder disappears from the listing.\n17: \n18: > Spec folder: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default`\n19: \n20: &nbsp;\n21: \n22: ## Why This Release\n23: \n24: Claude Code showed 32 of the 44 tracked commands. The create folder held a file named `skill.md` beside twelve other commands. Claude read the folder as one skill named `create`, so those twelve names never appeared.\n25: \n26: The cause is an open bug in Claude Code (`anthropics/claude-code#85786`). It holds for any capitalisation of `skill.md` and on any filesystem. The only documented way out is another file name. So no command file may carry that name now.\n27: \n28: An alias would keep a `skill.md` file alive, and the bug with it. The old name is retired with no alias, on every runtime.\n29: \n30: &nbsp;\n31: \n32: ## What's New at a Glance\n33: \n34: - **The command is now `/create:sk-skill`.** The typed, plain and slash variants all reach it. The old name reaches nothing. <!-- section: Create Skill Command -->\n35: - **No live file spells the old name.** Command files, catalogs, hub metadata, docs and runtime stubs carry the new name. <!-- section: Create Skill Command -->\n36: - **Mode and asset names stay.** The `sk-create-skill` packet, its folder and the `create-skill-*` asset files keep their names. <!-- section: Create Skill Command -->\n37: - **Claude Code lists all 44 commands.** Its create folder keeps `sk-skill.md` beside the twelve other commands. <!-- section: Claude Code Reach -->\n38: - **A `skill.md` file fails the mirror check now.** The check has no allowlist, and it looks at every capitalisation. <!-- section: Claude Code Reach -->\n39: \n40: &nbsp;\n41: \n42: ## Create Skill Command\n43: \n44: #### Type the New Name\n45: \n46: `/create:sk-skill` replaces `/create:skill` in the command file, its three assets, the two command catalogs and the sk-doc hub metadata. The command behaves as before. Only the name a reader types changed. The mode id, the packet folder and the `create-skill-*` asset file names keep their old spelling.\n47: \n48: #### Breaking: The Old Name Is Gone\n49: \n50: **Breaking:** A typed `/create:skill` now matches no tracked command. It reaches no command at all. Any script, saved prompt or doc that still names it needs the new spelling. There is no alias to fall back on.\n51: \n52: &nbsp;\n53: \n54: ## Claude Code Reach\n55: \n56: #### All 44 Commands Appear\n57: \n58: The regenerated Claude tree holds `create/sk-skill.md` and twelve siblings. No file under `.claude/commands` is named `skill.md` in any capitalisation. The runtime mirror check reads `visibility claude 44/44`, up from `32/44`.\n59: \n60: #### The Check Has No Exception\n61: \n62: The mirror check now fails any command folder that holds a `skill.md` file, whatever its capitalisation. Its old allowlist is gone. That stops a future command from bringing the collapsed folder back.\n63: \n64: &nbsp;\n65: \n66: ## How It Was Checked\n67: \n68: #### Before and After\n69: \n70: | Check | Before | After |\n71: |---|---|---|\n72: | `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check` | `visibility claude 32/44` | `visibility claude 44/44` |\n73: | Command files named `skill.md` in the Claude tree | 1 | 0 |\n74: | Entries in `.claude/commands/create` | 13, with `skill.md` | 13, with `sk-skill.md` |\n75: | Old-name scan outside the spec folders | 55 files | 9 published history files |\n76: \n77: #### Tests and Scenarios\n78: \n79: - **The runtime mirror check passes.** Nine cases pass and none fail. One case covers a folder with a capitalised `SKILL.md`.\n80: - **The compiled-route check passes.** All seven hubs resolve and all 55 served copies match their authored files.\n81: - **The command catalog check passes.** Every catalog and every hub metadata covers the command tree.\n82: - **The sk-doc parent check passes.** It reports no hard invariant broken and no warning.\n83: \n84: &nbsp;\n85: \n86: ## Upgrade Notes\n87: \n88: - **Scripts and docs that type `/create:skill`:** change them to `/create:sk-skill`. The old name answers nothing.\n89: - **Saved prompts and snippets:** retype the command, then confirm the create skill answers.\n90: - **Skill authors who copied the old command path:** point references at `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md`.\n91: - **Mode and asset names:** the `sk-create-skill` packet, its mode id and the `create-skill-*` asset files keep their names. Leave them as they are.","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog/v2.10.0.0.md, lines 1-91\n1: ---\n2: title: \"sk-doc v2.10.0.0, the create skill command is now sk-skill\"\n3: description: \"v2.10.0.0 renames `/create:skill` to `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime with no alias, so no command file is named `skill.md` and Claude Code lists all 44 tracked commands.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"sk-doc v2.10.0.0\"\n6:   - \"sk-doc 2.10.0.0\"\n7:   - \"create skill command rename\"\n8:   - \"sk-skill command name\"\n9: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n10: contextType: \"general\"\n11: version: 2.10.0.0\n12: ---\n13: \n14: # v2.10.0.0, The Create Skill Command Is Now sk-skill\n15: \n16: `/create:skill` is now `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime, with no alias. The old file name caused the bug. A command file named `skill.md` makes Claude Code read its folder as one skill. Every other command in that folder disappears from the listing.\n17: \n18: > Spec folder: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default`\n19: \n20: &nbsp;\n21: \n22: ## Why This Release\n23: \n24: Claude Code showed 32 of the 44 tracked commands. The create folder held a file named `skill.md` beside twelve other commands. Claude read the folder as one skill named `create`, so those twelve names never appeared.\n25: \n26: The cause is an open bug in Claude Code (`anthropics/claude-code#85786`). It holds for any capitalisation of `skill.md` and on any filesystem. The only documented way out is another file name. So no command file may carry that name now.\n27: \n28: An alias would keep a `skill.md` file alive, and the bug with it. The old name is retired with no alias, on every runtime.\n29: \n30: &nbsp;\n31: \n32: ## What's New at a Glance\n33: \n34: - **The command is now `/create:sk-skill`.** The typed, plain and slash variants all reach it. The old name reaches nothing. <!-- section: Create Skill Command -->\n35: - **No live file spells the old name.** Command files, catalogs, hub metadata, docs and runtime stubs carry the new name. <!-- section: Create Skill Command -->\n36: - **Mode and asset names stay.** The `sk-create-skill` packet, its folder and the `create-skill-*` asset files keep their names. <!-- section: Create Skill Command -->\n37: - **Claude Code lists all 44 commands.** Its create folder keeps `sk-skill.md` beside the twelve other commands. <!-- section: Claude Code Reach -->\n38: - **A `skill.md` file fails the mirror check now.** The check has no allowlist, and it looks at every capitalisation. <!-- section: Claude Code Reach -->\n39: \n40: &nbsp;\n41: \n42: ## Create Skill Command\n43: \n44: #### Type the New Name\n45: \n46: `/create:sk-skill` replaces `/create:skill` in the command file, its three assets, the two command catalogs and the sk-doc hub metadata. The command behaves as before. Only the name a reader types changed. The mode id, the packet folder and the `create-skill-*` asset file names keep their old spelling.\n47: \n48: #### Breaking: The Old Name Is Gone\n49: \n50: **Breaking:** A typed `/create:skill` now matches no tracked command. It reaches no command at all. Any script, saved prompt or doc that still names it needs the new spelling. There is no alias to fall back on.\n51: \n52: &nbsp;\n53: \n54: ## Claude Code Reach\n55: \n56: #### All 44 Commands Appear\n57: \n58: The regenerated Claude tree holds `create/sk-skill.md` and twelve siblings. No file under `.claude/commands` is named `skill.md` in any capitalisation. The runtime mirror check reads `visibility claude 44/44`, up from `32/44`.\n59: \n60: #### The Check Has No Exception\n61: \n62: The mirror check now fails any command folder that holds a `skill.md` file, whatever its capitalisation. Its old allowlist is gone. That stops a future command from bringing the collapsed folder back.\n63: \n64: &nbsp;\n65: \n66: ## How It Was Checked\n67: \n68: #### Before and After\n69: \n70: | Check | Before | After |\n71: |---|---|---|\n72: | `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check` | `visibility claude 32/44` | `visibility claude 44/44` |\n73: | Command files named `skill.md` in the Claude tree | 1 | 0 |\n74: | Entries in `.claude/commands/create` | 13, with `skill.md` | 13, with `sk-skill.md` |\n75: | Old-name scan outside the spec folders | 55 files | 9 published history files |\n76: \n77: #### Tests and Scenarios\n78: \n79: - **The runtime mirror check passes.** Nine cases pass and none fail. One case covers a folder with a capitalised `SKILL.md`.\n80: - **The compiled-route check passes.** All seven hubs resolve and all 55 served copies match their authored files.\n81: - **The command catalog check passes.** Every catalog and every hub metadata covers the command tree.\n82: - **The sk-doc parent check passes.** It reports no hard invariant broken and no warning.\n83: \n84: &nbsp;\n85: \n86: ## Upgrade Notes\n87: \n88: - **Scripts and docs that type `/create:skill`:** change them to `/create:sk-skill`. The old name answers nothing.\n89: - **Saved prompts and snippets:** retype the command, then confirm the create skill answers.\n90: - **Skill authors who copied the old command path:** point references at `.skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md`.\n91: - **Mode and asset names:** the `sk-create-skill` packet, its mode id and the `create-skill-*` asset files keep their names. Leave them as they are."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog/v2.10.0.0.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794586012642,"end":1794586013082}}}}
