{"type":"text","timestamp":1794586057894,"sessionID":"ses_e2a5adb61ffe5JLlq3JICE94gJ","part":{"id":"prt_1d5aa06df0012oNatzP6M18Wnd","sessionID":"ses_e2a5adb61ffe5JLlq3JICE94gJ","messageID":"msg_1d5a9ebdb0015BYLLSCohpZl93","type":"text","text":"T026 is done. The changelog entry exists at the resolved `sk-doc` parent target, with the four hub version fields bumped to `2.10.0.0`.\n\n**Files written**\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog/v2.10.0.0.md` (new, expanded format for the breaking change)\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/SKILL.md` (version field only, `2.9.13.0` to `2.10.0.0`)\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/hub-router.json` (version field only)\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/mode-registry.json` (version field only)\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/description.json` (version field only)\n\nThe entry opens with the break: `/create:skill` is now `/create:sk-skill` on every runtime, with no alias, because a command file named `skill.md` makes Claude Code read its folder as one skill. It carries a `**Breaking:**` H4, a before-and-after table, four test results and upgrade notes. It follows the `sk-create-changelog` workflow: template read, target resolved through `.skilled/changelog/sk-doc/parent`, version chosen as the minor bump to `2.10.0.0`, shape and voice gates run, then the hub parent check.\n\n**Verify output**\n```\n$ git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- '*/changelog/*'\n?? .skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog/v2.10.0.0.md\n\n$ git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- .skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog .skilled/changelog\nexit=0\n\n$ node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/parent-skill-check.cjs .skilled/skills/sk-doc | tail -1\nOK: parent-skill-check — all hard invariants passed, 0 warnings\n```\n\n**Supporting gates**\n- `check_changelog_shape.py`: `PASS`, `files=1 pass=1 fail=0`.\n- `hvr_scan.py`: 0 hard blockers, 100/100 mechanical ceiling.\n- `validate_document.py`: `VALID`, 0 issues.\n- Entry body is 91 lines, under the 280-line expanded ceiling.\n\n**Notes**\n- No upstream branch is configured, so the workflow's rule applied: the version was numbered locally and no collision exists on `origin/main`.\n- The entry cites only evidence I ran or that `scratch/before.txt` recorded. The holdout gain belongs to the intent-phrase lane in another component, so the entry does not claim it.\n- Secondary components touched by the phase, `system-skill-advisor` and `system-spec-kit`, are candidates for their own entries. I wrote no extra file for them, per the workflow.\n- Nothing I could not do. `tasks.md` was not ticked, as instructed.\n\nNothing is blocked on the operator. The coordinator owns the T026 tick and the remaining verification tasks.","time":{"start":1794586052319,"end":1794586057894}}}
